{"event_type":"review","id":"ec84c1b53432b7f6665092b0dea3c1daecfabb4cff7ebe9db7892fbe2b456a61","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T17:39:04Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/928f424323764b3b15317efd75c5ece857165636bd70fdf7273b6d7606a40702","sha256":"928f424323764b3b15317efd75c5ece857165636bd70fdf7273b6d7606a40702"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/30e4862fcb0056016556a0e5258b1a4e596b550c1882d41805bd737aa11f06d2","sha256":"30e4862fcb0056016556a0e5258b1a4e596b550c1882d41805bd737aa11f06d2"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a1d8682a102ae8a34f89e03a249882b54156ecf20bc9898fc8cbf36bbfa9616b","sha256":"a1d8682a102ae8a34f89e03a249882b54156ecf20bc9898fc8cbf36bbfa9616b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e9747be3fe82fbfa2b596c1bb5cf60f402d7803dbb06752866c27aad62343c30","sha256":"e9747be3fe82fbfa2b596c1bb5cf60f402d7803dbb06752866c27aad62343c30"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/fd425c95623cfec72195707cbd5d2c3751cc0b8cdcebd6566e950c57ca8537a0","sha256":"fd425c95623cfec72195707cbd5d2c3751cc0b8cdcebd6566e950c57ca8537a0"}],"attempt_id":"ec5d1927dca399e66243922a5f2e3b99cc19580d6f8b1d25d9584b222bc30d4c:0:1","base":"74dc99b5dc88590e26040c8fbb10698306bd2153","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"739423a86ad6219d96be2488d7c8210d3b677c01","body":"**`test/global-setup.test.ts:66`: Use `fileURLToPath` instead of `URL.pathname` to compute the root.**\n\nOn Windows, `new URL(...).pathname` returns a path like `/C:/...`. It also leaves percent-encoded characters in place. `test/global-setup.ts:16` already uses `fileURLToPath` for the same value. The test therefore resolves a different root from production on win32, and `readFileSync` fails there.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const root = new URL('..', import.meta.url).pathname;\n+  const root = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url));\n```\n\nAdd this import:\n\n```diff\n+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n```\n</details>","id":"223ab60705f11976dca48b989152aa80a88636d85e81768ac3e859251968b3de","intervals":[],"path":"test/global-setup.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`test/global-setup.test.ts:66`: Use `fileURLToPath` instead of `URL.pathname` to compute the root."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"c1a0377f42fc142c91850fec2a356a8decd878f9","body":"**Update the `fixReport` contract now that `headRefused` also omits it.**\n\nThe `headRefused` early return (Lines 944-957) returns no `fixReport`. The `fixReport` doc at Lines 521-525 still says it is absent \"ONLY\" for the step-2 truncated-classification refusal. A consumer that reads a missing `fixReport` as \"truncated\" will misreport a head refusal. Add the head refusal to that doc.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed doc fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   /**\n-   * The governed fix-run report. Absent ONLY when the loop refused before\n-   * the fix stage (the step-2 truncated-classification refusal) — no fix\n+   * The governed fix-run report. Absent ONLY when the loop refused before\n+   * the fix stage (the `headRefused` expected-head refusal, or the step-2\n+   * truncated-classification refusal) — no fix\n```\n</details>","id":"2e6140ac2e1581c7e6871a2666e1bdd58b08a379415bc5aeb874dd22a19e37af","intervals":[],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Update the `fixReport` contract now that `headRefused` also omits it."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"c1a0377f42fc142c91850fec2a356a8decd878f9","body":"**Exclude file-ordering waits from the per-job ladder.**\n\nIn engine-owned mode, `runLadder` starts before the wait at `src/plans/review-loop.ts:1162`. If the wait outlasts the ladder, the job can settle as `budget-exhausted` before its worker starts. If a sibling reported commits, this also withholds loop publication.\n\nMove the wait before the ladder. Preserve ordering after sibling failures and the pathless-item barrier.","id":"d3e39e26e91e0b480b4a689c97be75d477432b155dfab0f751706b21dc402989","intervals":[],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Exclude file-ordering waits from the per-job ladder."}],"head":"0f1ee5ca0b3b9f5dec57eac044c0dce3260d796d","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"c1a0377f42fc142c91850fec2a356a8decd878f9","intervals":[[9,9],[12,15],[76,78],[96,98],[104,105],[108,109],[111,112],[114,116],[152,307],[367,368],[404,409],[465,485],[488,490],[495,501],[506,507],[560,567],[675,678],[772,821],[914,920],[940,941],[944,958],[1000,1076],[1097,1102],[1106,1108],[1124,1126],[1128,1217],[1219,1219],[1250,1250],[1260,1260],[1267,1267],[1440,1450],[1453,1460],[1463,1466],[1468,1472],[1480,1484],[1488,1497],[1569,1575],[1577,1621],[1623,1623],[1682,1683],[1696,1696],[1708,1708],[1728,1729]],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"},{"blob":"739423a86ad6219d96be2488d7c8210d3b677c01","intervals":[[2,5],[7,7],[22,37],[49,95]],"path":"test/global-setup.test.ts"},{"blob":"fae0e4067e25d2752559dbb4a2aa92759003efd6","intervals":[[1,2],[5,5],[7,12],[89,108]],"path":"test/global-setup.ts"},{"blob":"b139f7c01773b4923d795858e3e9cfb7911253bc","intervals":[[8,9],[14,19],[22,34],[40,40],[55,59],[68,68],[73,167],[189,247]],"path":"test/selfhost/config.test.ts"}],"job_id":"ec5d1927dca399e66243922a5f2e3b99cc19580d6f8b1d25d9584b222bc30d4c:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"9b31ba3acf99de9a4af89266ca59348aebacaace","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"},"merge":"d8da1e2f8a592f1858a1bf97cb04a729ce9f6d3b","method":"pre-merge","pre":"34401d741bd653d722472f4e99a1dca6040433ce","source_path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"